---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import MatrixDerivation from '../components/MatrixDerivation.svelte';
---

<Layout title="Generator matrix — Error Detection & Subnetting" description="Step-by-step derivation of the generator and parity-check matrices for a cyclic code.">
  <h1>Generator matrix</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    A CRC is a cyclic code, and every linear code has a generator matrix G whose rows span it. Below,
    G is built twice — first from shifts of g(x), then in systematic form where the message stays
    visible and the parity bits are exactly the CRC — followed by the parity-check matrix H and a
    proof that the two fit together.
  </p>
  <MatrixDerivation client:load />
</Layout>
